1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock — LeetCode 121

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:04,600
Problem: prices[i] is the stock price on day i. Buy once and sell later to maximise your profit.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,100
Example: prices = [7, 1, 5, 3, 6, 4]

4
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:10,000
Buy at 1, sell at 6 → max profit = 6 − 1 = 5

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,650
Hint: you must buy before you sell — so as you scan, remember the lowest price so far, the best day to have bought

6
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:19,550
Approach: one pass, two trackers — minPrice (lowest so far) and maxProfit (best price − minPrice)

7
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:24,100
Start: minPrice = infinity, maxProfit = 0

8
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:28,500
Day 0: price 7 is below minPrice, so minPrice = 7

9
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:32,410
Day 1: price 1 is a new low → buy at 1, minPrice = 1

10
00:00:32,410 --> 00:00:36,320
Day 2: price 5 → profit 5 − 1 = 4, better than 0 → maxProfit = 4

11
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:39,500
Day 3: price 3 → profit 2, not better, keep 4

12
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:43,410
Day 4: price 6 → profit 6 − 1 = 5, a new best → maxProfit = 5

13
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:46,590
Day 5: price 4 → profit 3, not better, keep 5

14
00:00:46,590 --> 00:00:48,990
maxProfit = 5 — buy at 1, sell at 6

15
00:00:48,990 --> 00:00:53,580
Buy low at 1, sell high at 6 → profit 5. Time O(n), space O(1)

16
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:58,700
